sequenceDiagram
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · started by proof:run
  %% kind: proof.command
  autonumber
  participant GW as Gateway
  participant SW as Swamp
  participant VM as Proof VM
  GW->>SW: Start one shard<br/>full intent
  %%> Record one group and VM with its whole batch assignments and expected expanded case ids. Operator proofs instead carry one full command from task admission. Record the run budget of the shard from its batches: 600 s, 180 s a batch and the measured case seconds, times 1.5, rounded up to five minutes, at most two hours.
  SW->>VM: Claim a slot
  SW->>VM: Read the workspace commit
  SW->>SW: Check the workspace commit
  %%> A mismatch fails before cases and records expected and found commits.
  loop assigned batches, one at a time
    SW->>VM: Restore the head checkout
    %%> A prior flagged-case check may have left the checkout at the merge base. Restore the admitted head before planning.
    SW->>VM: Plan the assigned batch
    %%> runner plan --lines --only-batch restricts execution to the whole admitted batch. An operator run plans the full command.
    SW->>VM: Restore the base snapshot
    SW->>VM: Run batch setup
    SW->>VM: Run batch cases
    %%> The runner schedules cases within the fleet's existing concurrency and isolation rules. Keep every verdict line in the output artifact.
    opt CI replay after every head case passed
      SW->>SW: Check head verdicts
      SW->>VM: Read runner capabilities
      %%> Read head runner help. Without replay support, skip selection and replay.
      SW->>VM: Check out the base
      SW->>VM: Select replay cases
      %%> Use the runner's case-level comparison, then keep fails_on_base: true. Unchanged flags and unflagged cases never replay, even under whole-file code or tooling selection.
      SW->>VM: Remove the base copy
      SW->>SW: Scope replay case ids
      %%> Keep only cases admitted to this batch.
      SW->>VM: Switch to the base
      SW->>VM: Read nested commit
      SW->>SW: Check nested commit
      SW->>VM: Take head case files
      %%> Copy cases, batches and the spec loader. Keep base runner and step implementations.
      SW->>VM: Restore base snapshot
      SW->>VM: Run replay setup
      SW->>VM: Run replay cases
      SW->>SW: Join replay verdicts
      %%> Each replay must fail with cause assertion. A pass, another cause or missing evidence fails the proof with a CASE@merge-base verdict. Keep flags after merge; only a later case change opts them into another replay.
    end
    VM-->>SW: Batch verdicts
    SW-->>GW: Batch run ended
    %%> The Gateway reads each ended batch run with the parent's reconcile and records its full report artifact on the shard, once.
  end
  SW->>VM: Release the slot
  %%> Always after success or failure. Only operator proofs can keep a failed VM for 60 minutes. CI always deletes.
  SW->>SW: Report<br/>full verdict artifact
  %%> Prefix each line with its command, file and batch. The fixed capture reads the full artifact rather than the 4 KiB history summary.
  SW-->>GW: Native terminal result
  GW->>GW: Record all expected cases
  %%> Failed, missing, duplicate or unassigned verdicts fail the shard. A missing case becomes unrun. A missing or failed delete schedules normal group cancellation. The parent closes one merged report after all shards end.
  %%> A shard that reaches its run budget is timed out: it keeps the recorded verdicts of the batches that ended, and only the cases of the other batches are unrun.
